MASTER PROMPT: DATA & CODE — BUSINESS AUTOMATION SYSTEM

1. Project Overview

Build a complete, professional, responsive, multi-tenant SaaS web application named:

Data & Code — Business Automation System

Brand tagline: Precision Data & Software Solutions

The platform will be developed and maintained by Data & Code. It will offer subscription-based business management software to multiple independent companies.

The application must support small businesses, medium-sized businesses and large businesses through one unified system. Each company can configure its own business profile, logo, employees, products, inventory, purchases, sales, accounting, customer dues, supplier payables, invoices, PDF documents and printed reports.

This must be a functional business application with persistent database storage, authentication, authorization, CRUD operations, calculations and reporting—not merely a UI prototype.

2. Mandatory Architecture: Multi-Tenant System

Implement a secure multi-tenant architecture.

- Each registered company must have a separate logical workspace and isolated business data.
- Every business record must be associated with its authorized company or tenant.
- One company must never be able to view, search, modify, export or delete another company's private records.
- Apply server-side authorization and database-level tenant isolation. If using Firebase, implement appropriate Security Rules and server-side validation. If using a relational database, implement suitable row-level security policies.
- Never rely solely on hiding menu items or frontend conditions for security.
- Each company must see only its own customers, suppliers, employees, products, purchases, sales, accounts, reports and uploaded files.
- The platform's Super Admin dashboard and administrative information must never be visible to company users.
- Data must persist after logout, refresh, device changes and subsequent login.
- Do not use browser localStorage as the primary database. Use it only for non-sensitive preferences or temporary interface state.
- Use secure cloud storage for company logos and uploaded documents.

3. User Registration and Access Approval

Create a public registration page where anyone can create an account using an email address or mobile number.

However, registration must NOT automatically grant access to a real company workspace.

Initial registration process

1. A user submits their name, email address and/or mobile number and creates login credentials.
2. The system creates an account with the status "GUEST" or "DEMO_PENDING".
3. The user can access only the public pages and authorized demo environment.
4. The user must not be able to access any real company's data.
5. The Super Admin reviews and approves the account.
6. The Super Admin associates the approved login identity with the appropriate company and assigns a role.
7. Only after authorization can the user access that company's workspace.

Use secure authentication. Verify email or mobile ownership through an appropriate supported verification method. Never treat an unverified email or phone number as proof of identity.

Demo access restrictions

- A guest can use the demo project without receiving access to a real company's database.
- Limit the guest to a maximum of five total demo business-record creations across the demo environment. Allow a configurable limit of three to five records.
- Enforce the limit on the server or database side so refreshing the page, changing browsers or modifying frontend code cannot bypass it.
- Display the remaining demo entries clearly.
- When the limit is reached, disable further demo record creation and display a professional message asking the user to request approval or a subscription.
- Demo data must be isolated from production data.
- Never allow demo users to create real companies, invite employees to real workspaces, change subscriptions or access Super Admin controls.

The Super Admin must be able to approve, reject, suspend or revoke access.

4. Super Admin Dashboard — Private Platform Administration

Create a separate, protected Super Admin dashboard for the platform owner.

The Super Admin dashboard must not appear in company dashboards or guest navigation.

Super Admin features

- Secure Super Admin login and role verification.
- Add, edit, activate, suspend and deactivate companies.
- Approve or reject guest and company access requests.
- Assign approved email addresses and mobile numbers to specific companies.
- Control which users can log in to each company's workspace.
- Assign and manage company owners and employees.
- Configure subscription plans, prices, limits and trial periods.
- Set subscription start and end dates.
- View subscription status, renewal dates and payment records.
- Manage demo limits and demo expiry.
- View company registration statistics and subscription summaries.
- Review security events, account status and audit logs.
- Revoke sessions and suspend unauthorized accounts.
- Configure platform-wide settings.

The Super Admin must be the only role authorized to create and activate a real company workspace.

Protect the Super Admin account through strong authentication and server-side authorization. Do not expose Super Admin credentials, private API keys or administrative secrets in frontend code.

