25. Development and Delivery Plan

Implement the project in stages while maintaining one coherent architecture.

Phase 1: Project foundation, branding, authentication, guest/demo registration, Super Admin security, company approval and tenant isolation.

Phase 2: Company profiles, logo uploads, subscription plans, expiry controls, employee accounts and permissions.

Phase 3: Products, inventory, purchases, sales, customer dues, supplier payables and transaction documents.

Phase 4: Accounting, expenses, cash and bank management, ledgers and financial reports.

Phase 5: PDF, printing, company-branded templates, multilingual interface and optional business-specific modules.

Phase 6: Security testing, tenant-isolation testing, accounting validation, mobile testing and deployment.

Before completing each phase, test the actual workflows and fix errors rather than merely presenting a visual mockup.

26. Acceptance Criteria

The application will be considered functional only when all the following tests pass:

1. A new user can register but receives only Guest/Demo access.
2. The demo user cannot access a real company's records.
3. The demo limit is enforced server-side.
4. Only an authorized Super Admin can activate a company.
5. Approved users can access only their assigned company.
6. Company A cannot access Company B's records, files, invoices or reports.
7. A company can upload and update its own logo.
8. The company profile automatically populates invoice and memo headers.
9. Credit sales correctly increase customer receivables.
10. Credit purchases correctly increase supplier payables.
11. Payments update the appropriate outstanding balances.
12. Purchases and sales update inventory correctly.
13. Finalized financial entries remain consistent and auditable.
14. PDF exports and printed documents contain the correct company information.
15. Expired subscriptions restrict access according to policy without deleting data.
16. Employees cannot access features outside their assigned permissions.
17. The platform's Super Admin dashboard remains private.
18. The system works on Android phones, desktop computers and modern browsers.

Start by establishing the architecture, database schema, authentication model, tenant security and core application shell. Then implement the actual modules and test each phase.

Final instruction: Build a secure, scalable and genuinely functional subscription-based Business Automation System for Data & Code. Prioritize data isolation, accurate business accounting, ease of use, company-specific branding and maintainability over decorative effects. Do not claim that a feature is complete until it has been implemented and tested.